Nothing related with binutils or gcc4. The problem was the extensive use=20
of kernel structures located under /usr/include/ by aboot. The kernel=20
maintainers decided to make a headers clean up (aka sanitized headers)=20
from userspace which broke aboot.

In this case, the errors would appear in compilation time. So I think=20
this is not your problem.

Good luck.

